            <div xml:id="d887">

                <pb facs="0707" n="591" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg591"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/12967.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Vice Consul Silliman.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-08-25">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 25, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your August 23, 9 p.m. The President will be pleased to render any assistance in
                    his power in securing a conference between the First Chief Carranza and Zapata.
                    You may say that this Government is ready to do all it can in every legitimate
                    way to advance the welfare of the people of Mexico and will be pleased to have
                    the First Chief consult freely and fully about any matter in which he thinks
                    assistance can be rendered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
